{%- comment -%}
  CAVIERA loader — final 2026 revision: a single walking-Oryx VIDEO
  (assets/caviera-loader-oryx-2026.mp4) over a full-screen Obsidian field, once per browsing
  session, homepage only. Rendered unconditionally via `{% render 'caviera-loader' %}` inside
  `{% if template.name == 'index' %}` in layout/theme.liquid — unchanged, not duplicated here.
  This is the ONLY loader implementation in the theme (no sections/caviera-loader.liquid exists —
  do not recreate one).

  Replaces the previous multi-stage image sequence (oryx walk → House Seal → Master Signature),
  which existed only as a placeholder while final motion artwork was pending (see git history) —
  the approved video is now the only visual event, per this round's explicit brief: no decorative
  graphics, no progress/spinner/loading bar, no House Seal or Master Signature here.

  The root element and the <video> itself always render unconditionally on the homepage —
  assets/caviera-loader.js and assets/caviera-loader.css decide at runtime whether it actually
  activates (respecting settings.enable_loader, prefers-reduced-motion, and the once-per-session
  sessionStorage flag), and the loader always fails open: if the script never runs, or the video
  fails/stalls/rejects autoplay, the homepage underneath is never blocked (see the script's own
  header comment for the exact safety paths).
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if settings.enable_loader -%}
  <div class="caviera-loader" data-caviera-loader aria-hidden="true">
    <video
      class="caviera-loader__video"
      data-loader-video
      src="{{ 'caviera-loader-oryx-2026.mp4' | asset_url }}"
      autoplay
      muted
      playsinline
      preload="auto"
    ></video>
  </div>
  <script src="{{ 'caviera-loader.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
{%- endif -%}
